 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1787). Words follow the Schirmer vocal score's spelling and punctuation (Va without its apostrophe; Leporello's O for Oh). In bar 15 the print has \"Va chi ti ho fatto\", a misprint for the libretto's \"Ma che ti ho fatto\"; the words follow the print (IPA of the printed letters), and singers sing \"Ma che\" (IPA ˈma ˈke). Leporello's runs of \"no\" and \"sì\" are the score's own repeats (the libretto has \"No, no\" once and no \"sì\"). IPA, word meanings and translations were drafted for this app (S33) and the IPA was checked against Castel. IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
